    "q-161721": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161721",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14147181/assets/6debac35386e085a0197cf9eb3f2da65cc719ace67163cad625f58c056fb8f67.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAA}}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?",
      "worked_solution": "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14147181/assets/c0b805c707981b9b6fcfa2ed387ad32a024fc845e6fd355a4b751ede4ad6a97e.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14147181/assets/69708aa698c38f8a29d3eb69083f893fd8fca183bd713387456624fc38b86fe9.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0<x<2,\\text{ }0<y<2\\}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
